  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "Done. Each project row now has a Delete button. It opens a confirmation dialog, and confirming removes the row and shows a \"Deleted “<name>”\" toast.\n\nI ran it in real Chromium at 375x812 and 1280x800, and `ULT-BROWSER: PASS (fail=0 warn=0 viewports=2)`. At both widths all 14 steps passed: open the dialog, Escape cancels, Delete removes the row (5 rows to 4), and the toast appears. After a cancel, focus returns to the same Delete button, and after a delete it moves to the nearest remaining row. I opened the 375px after-delete and 1280px dialog screenshots, and the long project names wrap without overflow. The 4 static tests pass. The report is `/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Ultimatum/918c00ce-8a04-5813-ba24-0f3d322bb563/scratchpad/live-o/br-t2/report.json`.\n\n- **Changes:** the work is in `app.js` and `styles.css`. It reuses the existing `Button`, `Dialog` and `Toast` components, and each Delete button's aria-label includes the project name.\n- **In-memory only:** the delete changes `window.PROJECTS` in memory, so a reload brings the rows back. The app has no backend or storage.\n- **Not verified:** axe wasn't available, so the accessibility check used the fallback only. I also didn't test the empty list or the 320px width.",
